    "https://careers.cqu.edu.au/job/Rockhampton-Lecturer-Paramedicine-QLD/1360570066/": {
      "title": "Lecturer",
      "description": "Lecturer - Paramedicine Job Details | Central Queensland University Skip to main content Home Jobs at CQUni Working at CQUni Candidate Profile Search by Keyword Search by Location Clear Home Jobs at CQUni Working at CQUni Candidate Profile Employee Login Search by Keyword Search by Location Show More Options Loading... Location All Department All State All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Lecturer - Paramedicine Posting Date: 22 Sept 2026 Type of Position: Continuing Location: Rockhampton, QLD, AU Townsville, QLD, AU Cairns, QLD, AU About this Opportunity Continuing, Full-Time School of Health, Medical and Applied Sciences Expected commencement November 2026 CQUniversity Cairns, Townsville or Rockhampton Total Remuneration $138,968 to $161,953 pa (including salary of $117,430 to $136,853 plus 17% superannuation and leave loading) Join an organisation with an unbreakable belief that quality education, training and research should be available to everyone – regardless of background, location or life circumstances. Make a difference in the next generation of paramedics Are you ready to make a meaningful impact through your academic expertise, industry experience and passion for teaching? CQUniversity is seeking two motivated Lecturers in Paramedicine to join our collaborative team and help shape the next generation of paramedics. Our School of Health, Medical and Applied Sciences delivers in-demand qualifications in a supportive, research-led environment. The Bachelor of Paramedicine , accredited by the Paramedicine Board of Australia, provides students with a strong foundation for a career in paramedicine. As a Lecturer, you will design and deliver engaging learning experiences across lectures, simulation and clinical-focused activities. You’ll bring your industry expertise into the classroom, support students on campus and in the field, and contribute to curriculum development, unit coordination, research and scholarship. Additionally, you may be required to lead and manage the Work Integrated Learning (WIL) portfolio, including curriculum design, industry and community partnerships, and student placements, while coordinating and teaching WIL units across online delivery modes. Through simulation, clinical learning and engaging teaching, you’ll help students build the practical skills and confidence they need to succeed as paramedics. Access to leading facilities and strong professional networks will support your teaching and ongoing professional development. Be Rewarded 17% superannuation (with the choice to join an award-winning superfund) 5.4 weeks annual leave (plus 3 working days paid at Christmas and New Year closure) 10 days personal/sick leave, plus 5 days carer’s leave 7.25 hours engaged service leave Fantastic professional and career development opportunities Up to 26 weeks (six months) paid parental leave Access to an Employee Assistance Program and Fitness Passport Position Requirements Completion of an undergraduate degree in Paramedicine, with postgraduate qualifications highly regarded. Teaching qualification or willingness to complete a Graduate Certificate in Tertiary Teaching / Education. Proven ability to contribute to curriculum development, writing and evaluation, particularly using flexible modes of delivery. Experience teaching and supervising undergraduate and postgraduate students, across a range of learning environments. Strong capacity to engage and collaborate effectively with industry partners, community stakeholders, and professional networks. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to contribute positively to team culture and academic collaboration. Experience in the development and delivery of low to high-fidelity clinical simulation ( highly desirable ). Position Description For further information about this position, please refer to the Position Description. Apply today for a career that changes lives Applications Close: 11:59pm, Tuesday, 20 October 2026 Job Requisition ID: 7281 Contact Details: Timothy Makrides (03) 9616 0570 t.makrides2@cqu.edu.au When submitting your application, please include: Your Current CV or Resume, and a 1-2 page Cover Letter highlighting your relevant skills, experience and suitability for the position. Work Rights: Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Candidates must hold the full rights to work in Australia to be considered for this appointment. CQUniversity is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes diversity in the workplace. Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, and CQUniversity’s domestic and international student graduates with post-study work rights are encouraged to apply. #ACADB || #LI-LM1 || #LI-Remote || Keywords: Academic Lecturer | Applied Research | Ambulance Training | Clinical Simulation | Clinical Supervision | Curriculum Development | Emergency Medical Care | Emergency Medicine Educator | First Responder Academic | Higher Education Teaching | Industry Engagement | Lecturer Paramedicine | Paramedic Science | Paramedic Education | Tertiary Education | Unit Coordinator | University Lecturer Apply now » Find similar jobs: All Jobs, Academic & ELICOS Jobs Disclaimer Accessibility Feedback Policy Privacy Right to Information Contact Us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. CRICOS Provider Code: 00219C   RTO Code 40939   CQUniversity Australia is a trading name of Central Queensland University."
