    "https://careers.cqu.edu.au/job/Rockhampton-Casual-Academic-Learning-Adviser-%28ITAP%29-QLD/1357966266/": {
      "title": "Position Requirements",
      "description": "Casual Academic Learning Adviser (ITAP) Job Details | Central Queensland University Skip to main content Home Jobs at CQUni Working at CQUni Candidate Profile Search by Keyword Search by Location Clear Home Jobs at CQUni Working at CQUni Candidate Profile Employee Login Search by Keyword Search by Location Show More Options Loading... Location All Department All State All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Casual Academic Learning Adviser (ITAP) Posting Date: 21 Sept 2026 Type of Position: Casual Location: Rockhampton, QLD, AU Mackay, QLD, AU Gladstone, QLD, AU Negotiable, AU Emerald, QLD, AU Bundaberg, QLD, AU Townsville, QLD, AU Cairns, QLD, AU About this Opportunity Casual Office of the Vice-President Indigenous Engagement CQUniversity  Bundaberg, Cairns, Emerald, Gladstone, Mackay, Rockhampton, or Townsville (Negotiable – Excluding SEQ) Casual Rates Apply Join an organisation with an unbreakable belief that quality education, training and research should be available to everyone – regardless of background, location or life circumstances. Working at CQUniversity CQUniversity is seeking dedicated Casual Learning Advisers to provide tailored tutorial assistance to Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander students through the Indigenous Tutorial Assistance Program (ITAP). In this rewarding role, you will deliver personalised academic support to students enrolled in SUN, STEPS, undergraduate and postgraduate programs across a range of disciplines. By mentoring students and strengthening their academic capability, you will contribute to improved learning outcomes and help foster a culturally safe, inclusive and supportive learning environment. This is a meaningful opportunity to use your expertise to empower students, build confidence and support success throughout their academic journey. Please note this is a casual pool. Your expression of interest will remain valid until 30 October 2026. You will only be contacted if appropriate casual work becomes available whilst your application is active. Position Requirements A completed qualification at the level at which you are tutoring. i.e., a minimum bachelor’s degree to tutor students studying within a Bachelor level course. Demonstrated knowledge and understanding of Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander cultures and societies, and the ability to communicate sensitively and effectively Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people and communities. Currently hold a Blue Card (Working with Children Positive Notice) to comply with the Working with Children (Risk Management and Screening) Act 2000 for regulated employment in education and care services. Apply today for a career that changes lives Applications Close: 11:59pm, Friday, 30 October 2026 Job Requisition ID: 7061 Contact Details: Linda Born ISP@cqu.edu.au When submitting your application, please include: Your Current CV or Resume, Certified copies of your qualifications, Certified copy of your Working with Children Check (Blue Card) and the names and email contact details of 2 referees. Work Rights: Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Candidates must hold the full rights to work in Australia to be considered for this appointment. CQUniversity is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes diversity in the workplace. Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people are encouraged to apply. #CASUAL || #LI-LM1 || #LI-Hybrid || Keywords: Academic Tutor | University Tutor | Higher Education Tutor | Student Success Adviser | Academic Skills Adviser | Learning Support Officer | Study Support Tutor | Education Support Officer | Academic Mentor | Indigenous Student Support Officer | First Nations Student Support Officer | Academic Coach | Sessional Academic | Study Skills Facilitator | Tertiary Support Officer Apply now » Find similar jobs: All Jobs, Academic & ELICOS Jobs Disclaimer Accessibility Feedback Policy Privacy Right to Information Contact Us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. CRICOS Provider Code: 00219C   RTO Code 40939   CQUniversity Australia is a trading name of Central Queensland University."
