    "https://careers.cqu.edu.au/job/Negotiable-Associate-Professor-Professor-Psychology/1331597366/": {
      "title": "Associate Professor / Professor",
      "description": "Associate Professor / Professor - Psychology Job Details | Central Queensland University Skip to main content Home Jobs at CQUni Working at CQUni Candidate Profile Search by Keyword Search by Location Clear Home Jobs at CQUni Working at CQUni Candidate Profile Employee Login Search by Keyword Search by Location Show More Options Loading... Location All Department All State All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Associate Professor / Professor - Psychology Posting Date: 15 Oct 2026 Type of Position: Continuing Location: Negotiable, AU About this Opportunity Continuing, Full-Time School of Health, Medical and Applied Sciences Flexible location options (excluding Southeast Queensland), with hybrid and work-from-home arrangements available – please detail in your cover letter your preferred location Associate Professor (Level D) – Total Remuneration $196,588 to $214,609 pa (including salary of $166,120 to $181,348 plus 17% superannuation and leave loading) Professor (Level E) – Total Remuneration $247,655 pa (including salary of $209,272 plus 17% superannuation and leave loading) One position available. Appointment level will be based on the attributes and experience of the successful candidate. Please indicate your preferred level in your application. Join an organisation with an unbreakable belief that quality education, training and research should be available to everyone – regardless of background, location or life circumstances. Working at CQUniversity Lead the delivery of programs that inspire the next generation of psychologists, prepare graduates for safe, ethical and evidence-based practice, and make a meaningful difference in the community. We are seeking an academic leader to drive excellence across our postgraduate professional programs, Master of Clinical Psychology, Master of Clinical Psychology (Advanced Entry), and Master of Professional Psychology programs , and play a key role in shaping the future of psychology education. In this position, you will lead curriculum design, accreditation compliance and teaching excellence, while fostering a culture of innovation and collaboration in clinical training. The priority for this position will be leadership in curriculum and teaching, with scope to engage in research and research higher degree supervision. The appointment may be made at Associate Professor (Level D) or Professor (Level E), depending on your experience and achievements. As Associate Professor , you will provide academic leadership across teaching, research translation, clinical training and professional practice. You will lead curriculum development, evaluate and enhance program quality, and ensure alignment with APAC accreditation standards and national benchmarks. You will contribute to strategic initiatives and work collaboratively with senior leaders and relevant committees to support academic excellence and continuous improvement. As Professor , you will be a recognised leader in psychology education and training, providing strategic direction across our postgraduate psychology programs. You will shape curriculum innovation and clinical training, influence educational and accreditation policy, mentor academic staff, and lead multidisciplinary teams. You will build and strengthen national and international partnerships to advance psychology education, research translation and professional practice. Be Rewarded 17% superannuation (with the choice to join an award-winning superfund) 5.4 weeks annual leave (plus 3 working days paid at Christmas and New Year closure) 10 days personal/sick leave, plus 5 days carer’s leave 7.25 hours engaged service leave Fantastic professional and career development opportunities Up to 26 weeks (six months) paid parental leave Access to an Employee Assistance Program and Fitness Passport Position Requirements Doctoral qualification (PhD or equivalent) in psychology, plus a Masters-level qualification meeting registration requirements OR a professional doctorate combining these elements. General registration with Ahpra as a Psychologist. Demonstrated ability to mentor colleagues and foster a culture of excellence; at Level E, proven capability to lead multidisciplinary teams and contribute to strategic planning. Strong (Level D) or distinguished (Level E) record of teaching excellence, with leadership in innovative online and blended pedagogy. Growing (Level D) or established (Level E) research profile, with evidence of research impact, high-quality publications, competitive funding, and supervision of honours and postgraduate students. Demonstrated experience in professional and community engagement, with evidence of scholarly and professional impact; at Level E, recognised disciplinary authority with significant influence across the profession and academia. Pre-Employment Checks Appointment to this role is subject to satisfactory pre-employment checks, which may include a National Police Check and/or Working with Children Check (where applicable). The University is committed to providing a safe, inclusive and respectful environment where its members can study, work and live free from gender-based violence. In line with our organisational values and regulatory obligations, applicants may be required to declare any past or current allegations, investigations or findings relating to gender-based violence. The successful candidate may also be required to demonstrate that they meet the “fit and proper person” criteria as required under applicable legislation and regulatory frameworks (including ASQA requirements where relevant). Our Commitment to Inclusion At CQUniversity, inclusivity is at the heart of who we are. We are committed to creating a workplace where everyone feels respected, supported and empowered to succeed regardless of background or ability. We advance reconciliation through our Stretch Reconciliation Action Plan (RAP), First Nations Workforce Strategy and our First Nations Cultural Competency Framework , strengthening opportunities for First Nations peoples and embedding cultural respect across our organisation. Through our Disability-Informed Action Plan, we continue to enhance accessibility and inclusion across our University. As a recognised member of the Hidden Disabilities Sunflower Program , we actively promote awareness and understanding of non-visible disabilities, helping to ensure everyone can bring their whole selves to work and thrive. CQUniversity is also committed to providing an accessible, equitable and inclusive recruitment and selection process. The University will provide reasonable adjustments throughout the recruitment, selection, appointment and onboarding process to ensure people with disability can participate on an equal basis with others. Position Description For further information about this position, please refer to the relevant position description: Associate Professor - Academic Level D Professor - Academic Level E Apply today for a career that changes lives To find out more about these roles, or for a confidential chat about how to apply, please email Dr Kathryn Buller of CAMPUS RADAR JOBS at kathryn@campusradarjobs.com. To apply, we request the following documents: A 1-page Cover Letter briefly addressing your suitability for the position; Your current academic CV; Your responses to the Selection Criteria (no more than 4 pages). Please indicate your preferred location in your cover letter. Applications Close: 11:59pm, Sunday, 15 November 2026 Job Requisition ID: 6745 Please note, applicants for the position must have full time work rights. CQUniversity is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes diversity in the workplace. Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, and CQUniversity’s domestic and international student graduates with post-study work rights are encouraged to apply. #ACADC || #LI-LM1 || #LI-Hybrid || Keywords: Clinical Psychologist | Clinical Psychology | Neuropsychologist | Counselling Psychologist | Forensic Psychologist | Registered General Psychologist | Clinical Supervisor | Provisional Psychologist Supervisor | Psychology Lecturer | Psychology Academic | University Teaching | Mental Health Clinician | Public Mental Health | Private Practice | Hospital Psychology | Child And Adolescent Mental Health | Positive Psychology | CBT | Therapist | Psychopathology | Mental Health Practitioner | Regional And Rural Psychology | Postgraduate Psychology Programs | Evidence-Based Practice | Psychotherapy | Trauma-Informed Practice | Clinical Research | PhD Psychology | APAC Accreditation | Academic Leadership Apply now » Find similar jobs: All Jobs, Academic & ELICOS Jobs Disclaimer Accessibility Feedback Policy Privacy Right to Information Contact Us Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. CRICOS Provider Code: 00219C   RTO Code 40939   CQUniversity Australia is a trading name of Central Queensland University."
